<title>UK: Charterhouse to launch 800 million stg buyout fund.</title>
<headline>Charterhouse to launch 800 million stg buyout fund.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Charterhouse Development Capital, the venture capital arm of Charterhouse Bank, is launching an 800 million stg buyout fund, the Sunday Telegraph reported.</p>
<p>The report said the fund would invest in established businesses across Europe. The minimum deal was likely to be 50 million stg including debt financing and about 60 percent is expected to go on British deals.</p>
<p>Major backers include Commercial Union, Metropolitan Life, the US Life assurance company, and American state pension funds, the report said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
